/-!
# The untilt of a Huber pair along an ideal of `𝕎 R⁺`

Let `(R, R⁺)` be a Huber pair and `J` an ideal of the Witt vectors `𝕎 R⁺`. The *untilt* of
`(R, R⁺)` along `J` is the ring `A = (𝕎 R⁺ ⧸ J)[1/[ϖ]]`, where `ϖ ∈ R⁺` is a pseudouniformiser
of `R` and `[ϖ]` its Teichmüller representative, with the topology in which the image `A⁺` of
`𝕎 R⁺ ⧸ J` is open and carries its `[ϖ]`-adic topology. When `(R, R⁺)` is a perfectoid Tate pair
of characteristic `p` and `J` is generated by a primitive element `ξ`, Scholze shows that
`(A, A⁺)` is a perfectoid Tate pair with tilt `(R, R⁺)`, and that every perfectoid Tate pair
with tilt `(R, R⁺)` arises in this way (*Étale cohomology of diamonds*, Theorem 3.17); for
instance `J = (p)` gives back `(R, R⁺)`, and `R = ℂ_p♭`, `J = (p - [p♭])` gives `(ℂ_p, 𝒪_{ℂ_p})`.
This file constructs `A` and `A⁺`, makes `A` a Tate ring in which `A⁺` is open and bounded when
`R` is a Tate ring, and proves that `A` is complete and Hausdorff for `J = (ξ)` when `R` is a
perfect complete Hausdorff Tate ring of characteristic `p` and `ξ` is primitive. It also constructs
the sharp map `♯_J : R → A`, the multiplicative map sending `x ∈ R⁺` to the class of `[x]`, from
which Scholze's identification of `R` with the tilt of `A` is built.

To make the ring independent of a choice of `ϖ`, `TauCeti.Perfectoid.untilt p P J` is defined as
the localisation of `𝕎 R⁺ ⧸ J` at the classes of the Teichmüller representatives `[a]` of all
`a ∈ R⁺` which are units of `R`. Every such `a` divides a power of any pseudouniformiser `ϖ ∈ R⁺`,
so this is a localisation of `𝕎 R⁺ ⧸ J` away from the class of `[ϖ]`, for every pseudouniformiser
`ϖ ∈ R⁺` (`TauCeti.Perfectoid.untilt.isLocalizationAway`). For a Tate ring `R` the untilt carries
the `[ϖ]`-adic topology `TauCeti.Huber.awayTopology` for one such `ϖ`; the neighbourhoods of zero
then have basis `[ϖ]ⁿ A⁺` for every pseudouniformiser `ϖ ∈ R⁺`
(`TauCeti.Perfectoid.untilt.hasBasis_nhds_zero`), so the topology does not depend on the choice.
It makes the untilt a Tate ring in which `A⁺` is open and bounded and the class of `[ϖ]` is a
pseudouniformiser.

If `R` is a perfect complete Hausdorff Tate ring of characteristic `p` and `J = (ξ)` with `ξ`
primitive, then `R⁺` is perfect and `ϖ`-adically complete, and the class of `[ϖ]` is a
nonzerodivisor of `𝕎 R⁺ ⧸ (ξ)`, for which this quotient is adically complete
(`WittVector.IsDistinguished.isAdicComplete_quotient`). Hence `𝕎 R⁺ ⧸ (ξ)` embeds into the
untilt, and the untilt is Hausdorff and complete.

The multiplicative *sharp map* `x ↦ x♯` on `R⁺` sends `x` to the image of `[x]`, and *Fontaine's
map* `θ_J : 𝕎 R⁺ [1/[ϖ]] → A` is induced by the quotient map, with kernel generated by `J`; so
`A` is also `𝕎 R⁺ [1/[ϖ]] ⧸ J`. For `R` perfect of characteristic `p`, the untilt along `(p)` is
`R⁺[1/ϖ]`.

For a Tate ring `R`, every element of `R` is a quotient of an element of `R⁺` by an element of
`R⁺` which is a unit of `R`, and the Teichmüller representatives of the latter are inverted in the
untilt; so `x ↦ x♯` extends uniquely to a multiplicative map `♯_J : R → A`. It is not additive in
general. For `R` perfect of characteristic `p`, `♯_J` is continuous whenever `p` is topologically
nilpotent in `A` (`TauCeti.Perfectoid.untilt.continuous_sharp_of_isTopologicallyNilpotent`), and in
particular along `J = (ξ)` with `ξ` primitive (`TauCeti.Perfectoid.untilt.continuous_sharp`). If
moreover `ϖ` divides `ξ₀`, then `A⁺ ⧸ (♯ϖ) = 𝕎 R⁺ ⧸ (ξ, [ϖ]) = R⁺ ⧸ (ϖ)`.

The last isomorphism makes the untilt along a primitive `ξ` perfectoid. Choose a pseudouniformiser
`ϖ ∈ R⁺` with `ϖ ^ p ∣ ξ₀`. Then `(♯ϖ) ^ p ∣ p` in `A⁺`, and under `A⁺ ⧸ (♯ϖ) ≃ R⁺ ⧸ (ϖ)` and
`A⁺ ⧸ (♯ϖ ^ p) ≃ R⁺ ⧸ (ϖ ^ p)` Frobenius `A⁺ ⧸ (♯ϖ) → A⁺ ⧸ (♯ϖ ^ p)` becomes Frobenius of the
perfect ring `R⁺`, which is bijective. Since `A⁺` is open and bounded, the untilt is a perfectoid
Tate ring by Bhatt–Morrow–Scholze's criterion
`TauCeti.Perfectoid.IsPerfectoidTateRing.of_bijective_frobeniusModPow`.

## Main definitions

* `TauCeti.Perfectoid.untiltDenominators p P`: the Teichmüller representatives of the elements
  of `R⁺` that are units of `R`.
* `TauCeti.Perfectoid.untilt p P J`: the untilt of `P` along `J`.
* `TauCeti.Perfectoid.untiltPlus p P J`: its subring `A⁺`, the image of `𝕎 R⁺ ⧸ J`.
* `TauCeti.Perfectoid.untilt.sharpPlus p P J`: the multiplicative map `R⁺ → A`, `x ↦ x♯`.
* `TauCeti.Perfectoid.untilt.sharp p P J`: its extension, the sharp map `♯_J : R → A`, for a Tate
  ring `R`.
* `TauCeti.Perfectoid.untilt.theta J hϖ L`: Fontaine's map `θ_J : 𝕎 R⁺ [1/[ϖ]] → A`, and
  `TauCeti.Perfectoid.untilt.quotientMapEquiv : 𝕎 R⁺ [1/[ϖ]] ⧸ J ≃+* A`.
* `TauCeti.Perfectoid.untilt.spanPEquiv`: the untilt along `(p)` is `R⁺[1/ϖ]`.
* `TauCeti.Perfectoid.untilt.quotientEquivUntiltPlus : 𝕎 R⁺ ⧸ (ξ) ≃+* A⁺` for primitive `ξ`, and
  `TauCeti.Perfectoid.untilt.quotientSharpEquiv : A⁺ ⧸ (♯ϖ) ≃+* R⁺ ⧸ (ϖ)` when moreover
  `ϖ ∣ ξ₀`.

## Main results

* `TauCeti.Perfectoid.untilt.isLocalizationAway`: the untilt is `(𝕎 R⁺ ⧸ J)[1/[ϖ]]` for every
  pseudouniformiser `ϖ ∈ R⁺`.
* `TauCeti.Perfectoid.untilt.hasBasis_nhds_zero`: the neighbourhoods of zero have basis
  `[ϖ]ⁿ A⁺`, for every pseudouniformiser `ϖ ∈ R⁺`.
* `TauCeti.Perfectoid.untilt.instIsTateRing`: for a Tate ring `R`, the untilt is a Tate ring,
  with `TauCeti.Perfectoid.untilt.isOpen_untiltPlus`,
  `TauCeti.Perfectoid.untilt.isBounded_untiltPlus`,
  `TauCeti.Perfectoid.untilt.untiltPlus_le_powerBoundedSubring`, and
  `TauCeti.Perfectoid.untilt.isPseudoUniformizer_algebraMap`.
* `WittVector.IsPrimitive.coeff_zero_mem_radical`,
  `WittVector.IsPrimitive.exists_isPseudoUniformizer_pow_dvd_coeff_zero`: for primitive
  `ξ ∈ 𝕎 R⁺`, `ξ₀` lies in the radical of `(ϖ)` for every pseudouniformiser `ϖ ∈ R⁺`, and if `R` is
  perfect of characteristic `p`, some pseudouniformiser `ϖ` has `ϖ ^ p ∣ ξ₀`.
* `TauCeti.Perfectoid.untilt.mk_teichmuller_mem_nonZeroDivisors`,
  `TauCeti.Perfectoid.untilt.algebraMap_injective`: for `R` a perfect Tate ring of
  characteristic `p` and primitive `ξ`, `[ϖ]` is regular in `𝕎 R⁺ ⧸ (ξ)` and `𝕎 R⁺ ⧸ (ξ)`
  embeds into the untilt along `(ξ)`.
* `TauCeti.Perfectoid.untilt.isAdicComplete_quotient`,
  `TauCeti.Perfectoid.untilt.isAdicComplete_quotient_natCast`,
  `TauCeti.Perfectoid.untilt.isAdicComplete_untiltPlus_natCast`,
  `TauCeti.Perfectoid.untilt.not_isUnit_untiltPlus_natCast`,
  `TauCeti.Perfectoid.untilt.t2Space`, `TauCeti.Perfectoid.untilt.completeSpace`: for `R` a
  perfect complete Hausdorff Tate ring of characteristic `p` and primitive `ξ`, `𝕎 R⁺ ⧸ (ξ)` and
  `A⁺` are `p`-adically complete, `p` is not a unit in `A⁺` when `A` is nontrivial, and the untilt
  along `(ξ)` is Hausdorff and complete.
* `TauCeti.Perfectoid.untilt.exists_algebraMap_eq`: every element of `A⁺` is the image of a Witt
  vector.
* `TauCeti.Perfectoid.untilt.sharp_dvd_algebraMap_iff`: for primitive `ξ` and `ϖ ∣ ξ₀`, `♯ϖ`
  divides the image of `a ∈ 𝕎 R⁺` in `A⁺` exactly when `ϖ` divides `a₀`.
* `TauCeti.Perfectoid.untilt.isPerfectoidTateRing`: for `R` a perfect complete Hausdorff Tate
  ring of characteristic `p` and primitive `ξ`, the untilt along `(ξ)` is a perfectoid Tate ring.
* `TauCeti.Perfectoid.untilt.ker_theta`: the kernel of `θ_J` is generated by `J`.
* `TauCeti.Perfectoid.untilt.sharp_apply`, `TauCeti.Perfectoid.untilt.sharp_unique`: `♯_J` is the
  unique multiplicative map sending `x ∈ R⁺` to the class of `[x]`.
* `TauCeti.Perfectoid.untilt.isPseudoUniformizer_sharp`: `♯_J` sends pseudouniformisers in `R⁺`
  to pseudouniformisers.
* `TauCeti.Perfectoid.untilt.sharp_eq_natCast`: `♯_J t = p` when `p - [t] ∈ J`.
* `TauCeti.Perfectoid.untilt.isTopologicallyNilpotent_natCast`,
  `TauCeti.Perfectoid.untilt.continuous_sharp_of_isTopologicallyNilpotent`,
  `TauCeti.Perfectoid.untilt.continuous_sharp`: for `R` a perfect Tate ring of characteristic `p`,
  `♯_J` is continuous whenever `p` is topologically nilpotent in the untilt, and in particular
  along `(ξ)` for primitive `ξ`.

## References

* P. Scholze, *Étale cohomology of diamonds*, Lemma 3.14 and Theorem 3.17 and its proof.
* P. Scholze and J. Weinstein, *Berkeley lectures on `p`-adic geometry*, Theorem 6.2.11.
* K. S. Kedlaya, *Sheaves, stacks, and shtukas*, Remark 2.3.3 and Theorem 2.3.9.
-/

public section

open Filter Topology TauCeti.Huber WittVector
open scoped nonZeroDivisors Pointwise

namespace TauCeti.Perfectoid

variable (p : ℕ) [Fact p.Prime] {R : Type*} [CommRing R]

local notation "𝕎" => WittVector p

section Topology

variable [TopologicalSpace R] [IsTopologicalRing R]

section Carrier

variable [IsHuberRing R] (P : Pair R)

/-- The denominators of the untilt: the Teichmüller representatives `[a] ∈ 𝕎 R⁺` of the elements
`a ∈ R⁺` which are units of `R`. -/
noncomputable def untiltDenominators : Submonoid (𝕎 P.plus) :=
  ((IsUnit.submonoid R).comap P.plus.subtype).map (teichmuller p)

variable {p P} in
@[simp]
theorem mem_untiltDenominators {x : 𝕎 P.plus} :
    x ∈ untiltDenominators p P ↔ ∃ a : P.plus, IsUnit (a : R) ∧ teichmuller p a = x := by
  simp [untiltDenominators, IsUnit.mem_submonoid_iff]

-- The local notation `𝕎` is not used in `variable` commands, where it does not elaborate.
variable (J : Ideal (WittVector p P.plus))

/-- **The untilt of a Huber pair `(R, R⁺)` along an ideal `J` of `𝕎 R⁺`**: the localisation of
`𝕎 R⁺ ⧸ J` at the classes of the Teichmüller representatives of the elements of `R⁺` which are
units of `R`. It is `(𝕎 R⁺ ⧸ J)[1/[ϖ]]` for every pseudouniformiser `ϖ ∈ R⁺`
(`TauCeti.Perfectoid.untilt.isLocalizationAway`). -/
def untilt : Type _ :=
  Localization ((untiltDenominators p P).map (Ideal.Quotient.mk J))

namespace untilt

noncomputable instance instCommRing : CommRing (untilt p P J) :=
  inferInstanceAs (CommRing (Localization ((untiltDenominators p P).map (Ideal.Quotient.mk J))))

noncomputable instance instAlgebra : Algebra (𝕎 P.plus ⧸ J) (untilt p P J) :=
  inferInstanceAs
    (Algebra (𝕎 P.plus ⧸ J) (Localization ((untiltDenominators p P).map (Ideal.Quotient.mk J))))

instance instIsLocalization :
    IsLocalization ((untiltDenominators p P).map (Ideal.Quotient.mk J)) (untilt p P J) :=
  inferInstanceAs (IsLocalization _
    (Localization ((untiltDenominators p P).map (Ideal.Quotient.mk J))))

variable {p P J}

/-- **The untilt is `(𝕎 R⁺ ⧸ J)[1/[ϖ]]`** for every pseudouniformiser `ϖ ∈ R⁺` of `R`. -/
theorem isLocalizationAway {ϖ : P.plus} (hϖ : IsPseudoUniformizer (ϖ : R)) :
    IsLocalization.Away (Ideal.Quotient.mk J (teichmuller p ϖ)) (untilt p P J) := by
  refine (IsLocalization.iff_of_le_of_exists_dvd (M := Submonoid.powers _)
    (N := (untiltDenominators p P).map (Ideal.Quotient.mk J)) ?_ ?_).mpr inferInstance
  · exact Submonoid.powers_le.mpr
      (Submonoid.mem_map_of_mem _ (mem_untiltDenominators.mpr ⟨ϖ, hϖ.isUnit, rfl⟩))
  · rintro _ ⟨_, hx, rfl⟩
    obtain ⟨a, ha, rfl⟩ := mem_untiltDenominators.mp hx
    obtain ⟨n, c, hc⟩ := P.plus.exists_dvd_pow_of_isTopologicallyNilpotent
      P.isRingOfIntegralElements.isOpen ha hϖ.isTopologicallyNilpotent
    refine ⟨_, ⟨n, rfl⟩, Ideal.Quotient.mk J (teichmuller p c), ?_⟩
    dsimp only
    rw [← map_pow, ← map_pow, hc, map_mul, map_mul]

end untilt

/-- **The subring `A⁺` of the untilt**: the image of `𝕎 R⁺ ⧸ J`. For a Tate ring `R` it is open
and bounded (`TauCeti.Perfectoid.untilt.isOpen_untiltPlus`,
`TauCeti.Perfectoid.untilt.isBounded_untiltPlus`); it is not claimed here to be integrally closed
in the untilt, which can fail for general `J`. -/
noncomputable def untiltPlus : Subring (untilt p P J) :=
  (algebraMap (𝕎 P.plus ⧸ J) (untilt p P J)).range

variable {p P J} in
@[simp]
theorem mem_untiltPlus {x : untilt p P J} :
    x ∈ untiltPlus p P J ↔ ∃ a : 𝕎 P.plus ⧸ J, algebraMap _ _ a = x :=
  RingHom.mem_range

end Carrier

namespace untilt

variable {p} [IsTateRing R] {P : Pair R} {J : Ideal (WittVector p P.plus)}

/-- For a unit `s` and a topologically nilpotent `t` of `R` in `R⁺`, every neighbourhood
`[s]ᵐ A⁺` contains some `[t]ᵏ A⁺`. -/
private theorem exists_awayNhd_subset {s t : P.plus} (hs : IsUnit (s : R))
    (ht : IsTopologicallyNilpotent (t : R)) (m : ℕ) :
    ∃ k, (awayNhd (Ideal.Quotient.mk J (teichmuller p t)) (untilt p P J) k : Set (untilt p P J)) ⊆
      awayNhd (Ideal.Quotient.mk J (teichmuller p s)) (untilt p P J) m := by
  obtain ⟨k, c, hc⟩ := P.plus.exists_dvd_pow_of_isTopologicallyNilpotent
    P.isRingOfIntegralElements.isOpen (a := s ^ m) (by simpa using hs.pow m) ht
  refine ⟨k, fun x hx ↦ ?_⟩
  obtain ⟨a, rfl⟩ := mem_awayNhd.mp hx
  refine mem_awayNhd.mpr ⟨Ideal.Quotient.mk J (teichmuller p c) * a, ?_⟩
  rw [← mul_assoc, ← map_pow, ← map_pow, ← map_mul, ← map_mul, ← hc, map_pow, map_pow]

variable (p P J) in
/-- **The topology of the untilt**: the `[ϖ]`-adic topology `TauCeti.Huber.awayTopology` on
`(𝕎 R⁺ ⧸ J)[1/[ϖ]]`, for a pseudouniformiser `ϖ ∈ R⁺` chosen by
`TauCeti.Huber.IsRingOfIntegralElements.exists_isPseudoUniformizer`. It does not depend on
the choice (`TauCeti.Perfectoid.untilt.hasBasis_nhds_zero`). -/
noncomputable instance instTopologicalSpace : TopologicalSpace (untilt p P J) :=
  @awayTopology _ _
    (Ideal.Quotient.mk J (teichmuller p
      P.isRingOfIntegralElements.exists_isPseudoUniformizer.choose))
    (untilt p P J) _ _
    (isLocalizationAway (ϖ := P.isRingOfIntegralElements.exists_isPseudoUniformizer.choose)
      P.isRingOfIntegralElements.exists_isPseudoUniformizer.choose_spec)

-- Here and in the instances below, the arguments of the `awayTopology` lemmas are given
-- explicitly: unification has to unfold `instTopologicalSpace` to `awayTopology`, which it does
-- not do while the pseudouniformiser is still a metavariable.
/-- The defining basis of the neighbourhoods of zero of the untilt, for the chosen
pseudouniformiser. -/
private theorem hasBasis_nhds_zero_choose :
    (𝓝 (0 : untilt p P J)).HasBasis (fun _ : ℕ ↦ True) fun n ↦
      (awayNhd (Ideal.Quotient.mk J (teichmuller p
        P.isRingOfIntegralElements.exists_isPseudoUniformizer.choose))
        (untilt p P J) n : Set (untilt p P J)) :=
  @hasBasis_nhds_zero_awayTopology _ _ _ (untilt p P J) _ _
    (isLocalizationAway (ϖ := P.isRingOfIntegralElements.exists_isPseudoUniformizer.choose)
      P.isRingOfIntegralElements.exists_isPseudoUniformizer.choose_spec)

/-- **The neighbourhoods of zero of the untilt have basis `[ϖ]ⁿ A⁺`**, for every
pseudouniformiser `ϖ ∈ R⁺` of `R`. In particular the topology of the untilt does not depend on
the choice of a pseudouniformiser. -/
theorem hasBasis_nhds_zero {ϖ : P.plus} (hϖ : IsPseudoUniformizer (ϖ : R)) :
    (𝓝 (0 : untilt p P J)).HasBasis (fun _ : ℕ ↦ True) fun n ↦
      (awayNhd (Ideal.Quotient.mk J (teichmuller p ϖ)) (untilt p P J) n : Set (untilt p P J)) :=
  have hϖ₀ := P.isRingOfIntegralElements.exists_isPseudoUniformizer.choose_spec
  hasBasis_nhds_zero_choose.to_hasBasis
    (fun m _ ↦ (exists_awayNhd_subset hϖ₀.isUnit hϖ.isTopologicallyNilpotent m).imp
      fun _ h ↦ ⟨trivial, h⟩)
    fun m _ ↦ (exists_awayNhd_subset hϖ.isUnit hϖ₀.isTopologicallyNilpotent m).imp
      fun _ h ↦ ⟨trivial, h⟩

variable (p P J)

/-- The untilt is a topological ring. -/
instance instIsTopologicalRing : IsTopologicalRing (untilt p P J) :=
  @isTopologicalRing_awayTopology _ _ _ (untilt p P J) _ _
    (isLocalizationAway (ϖ := P.isRingOfIntegralElements.exists_isPseudoUniformizer.choose)
      P.isRingOfIntegralElements.exists_isPseudoUniformizer.choose_spec)

/-- The untilt is a nonarchimedean ring. -/
instance instNonarchimedeanRing : NonarchimedeanRing (untilt p P J) :=
  @nonarchimedeanRing_awayTopology _ _ _ (untilt p P J) _ _
    (isLocalizationAway (ϖ := P.isRingOfIntegralElements.exists_isPseudoUniformizer.choose)
      P.isRingOfIntegralElements.exists_isPseudoUniformizer.choose_spec)

/-- **The untilt is a Tate ring**, with pair of definition `A⁺` and the class of `[ϖ]`. -/
instance instIsTateRing : IsTateRing (untilt p P J) :=
  haveI := isLocalizationAway (J := J)
    (ϖ := P.isRingOfIntegralElements.exists_isPseudoUniformizer.choose)
    P.isRingOfIntegralElements.exists_isPseudoUniformizer.choose_spec
  isTateRing_of_hasBasis hasBasis_nhds_zero_choose

/-- The uniform structure of the untilt: that of its additive topological group. -/
noncomputable instance instUniformSpace : UniformSpace (untilt p P J) :=
  IsTopologicalAddGroup.rightUniformSpace (untilt p P J)

/-- The untilt is a uniform additive group for `TauCeti.Perfectoid.untilt.instUniformSpace`. -/
instance instIsUniformAddGroup : IsUniformAddGroup (untilt p P J) :=
  isUniformAddGroup_of_addCommGroup

variable {p P J}

/-- The ring `A⁺` is open in the untilt. -/
theorem isOpen_untiltPlus : IsOpen (untiltPlus p P J : Set (untilt p P J)) :=
  isOpen_range_algebraMap_of_hasBasis hasBasis_nhds_zero_choose

/-- The ring `A⁺` is bounded in the untilt. -/
theorem isBounded_untiltPlus : IsBounded (untiltPlus p P J : Set (untilt p P J)) :=
  isBounded_range_algebraMap_of_hasBasis hasBasis_nhds_zero_choose

/-- Every element of `A⁺` is power-bounded in the untilt. -/
theorem untiltPlus_le_powerBoundedSubring :
    untiltPlus p P J ≤ powerBoundedSubring (untilt p P J) := fun _ hx ↦
  mem_powerBoundedSubring.mpr (isBounded_untiltPlus.isPowerBounded_of_mem hx)

/-- The class of the Teichmüller representative of a pseudouniformiser `ϖ ∈ R⁺` of `R` is a
pseudouniformiser of the untilt. -/
theorem isPseudoUniformizer_algebraMap {ϖ : P.plus} (hϖ : IsPseudoUniformizer (ϖ : R)) :
    IsPseudoUniformizer
      (algebraMap (𝕎 P.plus ⧸ J) (untilt p P J) (Ideal.Quotient.mk J (teichmuller p ϖ))) :=
  haveI := isLocalizationAway (J := J) hϖ
  isPseudoUniformizer_algebraMap_of_hasBasis (hasBasis_nhds_zero hϖ)

end untilt

end Topology

/-! ### Untilts along primitive elements -/

namespace untilt

section Primitive

variable {p} [TopologicalSpace R] [IsTopologicalRing R] [IsTateRing R] [CharP R p]
  [PerfectRing R p] {P : Pair R} {ξ : WittVector p P.plus}

omit [Fact p.Prime] [CharP R p] [PerfectRing R p] in
/-- The zeroth Witt coordinate of a primitive element lies in the radical of `(ϖ)`, for every
pseudouniformiser `ϖ ∈ R⁺`. -/
theorem _root_.WittVector.IsPrimitive.coeff_zero_mem_radical (hξ : ξ.IsPrimitive) {ϖ : P.plus}
    (hϖ : IsPseudoUniformizer (ϖ : R)) : ξ.coeff 0 ∈ (Ideal.span {ϖ}).radical := by
  obtain ⟨n, hn⟩ := P.plus.exists_dvd_pow_of_isTopologicallyNilpotent
    P.isRingOfIntegralElements.isOpen hϖ.isUnit
    (hξ.isTopologicallyNilpotent_coeff_zero.map (φ := P.plus.subtype) continuous_subtypeVal)
  exact ⟨n, Ideal.mem_span_singleton.mpr hn⟩

/-- For a primitive element `ξ`, some pseudouniformiser `ϖ ∈ R⁺` has `ϖ ^ p` dividing the zeroth
Witt coordinate of `ξ`: a power of `ξ₀` is divisible by a pseudouniformiser `ϖ₀`, and `R⁺` is
perfect, so a `p`-power root of `ϖ₀` will do. -/
theorem _root_.WittVector.IsPrimitive.exists_isPseudoUniformizer_pow_dvd_coeff_zero
    (hξ : ξ.IsPrimitive) :
    ∃ ϖ : P.plus, IsPseudoUniformizer (ϖ : R) ∧ ϖ ^ p ∣ ξ.coeff 0 := by
  have hp : p.Prime := Fact.out
  obtain ⟨ϖ₀, hϖ₀⟩ := P.isRingOfIntegralElements.exists_isPseudoUniformizer
  obtain ⟨n, hn⟩ := hξ.coeff_zero_mem_radical hϖ₀
  have hn' : ϖ₀ ∣ ξ.coeff 0 ^ p ^ n :=
    (Ideal.mem_span_singleton.mp hn).trans (pow_dvd_pow _ (Nat.lt_pow_self hp.one_lt).le)
  set ϖ := (iterateFrobeniusEquiv P.plus p (n + 1)).symm ϖ₀
  have hϖ : ϖ ^ p ^ (n + 1) = ϖ₀ := by
    rw [← iterateFrobeniusEquiv_def, RingEquiv.apply_symm_apply]
  have hϖp : (iterateFrobeniusEquiv P.plus p n).symm ϖ₀ = ϖ ^ p := by
    rw [RingEquiv.symm_apply_eq, iterateFrobeniusEquiv_def, ← pow_mul, ← pow_succ', hϖ]
  refine ⟨ϖ, ?_, ?_⟩
  · have hpow : (ϖ : R) ^ p ^ (n + 1) = ϖ₀ := by rw [← Subring.coe_pow, hϖ]
    have hne : p ^ (n + 1) ≠ 0 := pow_ne_zero _ hp.ne_zero
    exact isPseudoUniformizer_iff.mpr ⟨(isUnit_pow_iff hne).mp (hpow ▸ hϖ₀.isUnit),
      .of_pow hne (hpow ▸ hϖ₀.isTopologicallyNilpotent)⟩
  · have h := map_dvd (iterateFrobeniusEquiv P.plus p n).symm hn'
    rwa [hϖp, ← iterateFrobeniusEquiv_def, RingEquiv.symm_apply_apply] at h

/-- The class of `[ϖ]` is a nonzerodivisor of `𝕎 R⁺ ⧸ (ξ)` for primitive `ξ`. -/
theorem mk_teichmuller_mem_nonZeroDivisors (hξ : ξ.IsPrimitive) {ϖ : P.plus}
    (hϖ : IsPseudoUniformizer (ϖ : R)) :
    Ideal.Quotient.mk (Ideal.span {ξ}) (teichmuller p ϖ) ∈ (𝕎 P.plus ⧸ Ideal.span {ξ})⁰ :=
  hξ.isDistinguished.mk_teichmuller_mem_nonZeroDivisors (hξ.coeff_zero_mem_radical hϖ)
    (comap_nonZeroDivisors_le_of_injective (f := P.plus.subtype) Subtype.val_injective
      hϖ.isUnit.mem_nonZeroDivisors)

/-- **`𝕎 R⁺ ⧸ (ξ)` embeds into the untilt** along a primitive element `ξ`, for `R` a perfect Tate
ring of characteristic `p`: the class of `[ϖ]` is a nonzerodivisor. -/
theorem algebraMap_injective (hξ : ξ.IsPrimitive) :
    Function.Injective (algebraMap (𝕎 P.plus ⧸ Ideal.span {ξ}) (untilt p P (Ideal.span {ξ}))) :=
  have hϖ := P.isRingOfIntegralElements.exists_isPseudoUniformizer.choose_spec
  haveI := isLocalizationAway (J := Ideal.span {ξ}) hϖ
  IsLocalization.injective (M := Submonoid.powers _) _
    (Submonoid.powers_le.mpr (mk_teichmuller_mem_nonZeroDivisors hξ hϖ))

end Primitive

section Complete

variable {p} [UniformSpace R] [IsUniformAddGroup R] [IsTopologicalRing R] [IsTateRing R]
  [CompleteSpace R] [T2Space R] [CharP R p] [PerfectRing R p] {P : Pair R}
  {ξ : WittVector p P.plus}

/-- For a pseudouniformiser `ϖ ∈ R⁺`, the quotient `𝕎 R⁺ ⧸ (ξ)` is adically complete for the
class of `[ϖ]`. -/
theorem isAdicComplete_quotient (hξ : ξ.IsPrimitive) {ϖ : P.plus}
    (hϖ : IsPseudoUniformizer (ϖ : R)) :
    IsAdicComplete (Ideal.span {Ideal.Quotient.mk (Ideal.span {ξ}) (teichmuller p ϖ)})
      (𝕎 P.plus ⧸ Ideal.span {ξ}) :=
  haveI := IsUniform.of_perfectRing (R := R) p
  haveI := P.isRingOfIntegralElements.isAdicComplete_span_singleton ϖ hϖ
  hξ.isDistinguished.isAdicComplete_quotient (hξ.coeff_zero_mem_radical hϖ)

/-- For primitive `ξ`, the quotient `𝕎 R⁺ ⧸ (ξ)` is `p`-adically complete. -/
theorem isAdicComplete_quotient_natCast (hξ : ξ.IsPrimitive) :
    IsAdicComplete (Ideal.span {(p : 𝕎 P.plus ⧸ Ideal.span {ξ})})
      (𝕎 P.plus ⧸ Ideal.span {ξ}) :=
  have ⟨ϖ, hϖ⟩ := P.isRingOfIntegralElements.exists_isPseudoUniformizer
  haveI := IsUniform.of_perfectRing (R := R) p
  haveI := P.isRingOfIntegralElements.isAdicComplete_span_singleton ϖ hϖ
  hξ.isDistinguished.isAdicComplete_quotient_natCast (hξ.coeff_zero_mem_radical hϖ)

/-- `IsAdicComplete` instance for `(p)` on `𝕎 R⁺ ⧸ (ξ)` when `[Fact ξ.IsPrimitive]`. -/
instance instIsAdicCompleteQuotientNatCast [hξ : Fact ξ.IsPrimitive] :
    IsAdicComplete (Ideal.span {(p : 𝕎 P.plus ⧸ Ideal.span {ξ})})
      (𝕎 P.plus ⧸ Ideal.span {ξ}) :=
  isAdicComplete_quotient_natCast hξ.out

/-- **The untilt along a primitive element is Hausdorff**, for `R` a perfect complete Hausdorff
Tate ring of characteristic `p`. -/
theorem t2Space (hξ : ξ.IsPrimitive) : T2Space (untilt p P (Ideal.span {ξ})) :=
  have hϖ := P.isRingOfIntegralElements.exists_isPseudoUniformizer.choose_spec
  haveI := isLocalizationAway (J := Ideal.span {ξ}) hϖ
  haveI := isAdicComplete_quotient hξ hϖ
  t2Space_of_hasBasis (hasBasis_nhds_zero hϖ)
    (mk_teichmuller_mem_nonZeroDivisors hξ hϖ)

/-- **The untilt along a primitive element is complete**, for `R` a perfect complete Hausdorff
Tate ring of characteristic `p`. -/
theorem completeSpace (hξ : ξ.IsPrimitive) : CompleteSpace (untilt p P (Ideal.span {ξ})) :=
  have hϖ := P.isRingOfIntegralElements.exists_isPseudoUniformizer.choose_spec
  haveI := isLocalizationAway (J := Ideal.span {ξ}) hϖ
  haveI := isAdicComplete_quotient hξ hϖ
  completeSpace_of_hasBasis (hasBasis_nhds_zero hϖ)
    (mk_teichmuller_mem_nonZeroDivisors hξ hϖ)

/-- `T2Space` instance on `untilt p P (Ideal.span {ξ})` when `[Fact ξ.IsPrimitive]`. -/
instance instT2Space [hξ : Fact ξ.IsPrimitive] : T2Space (untilt p P (Ideal.span {ξ})) :=
  t2Space hξ.out

/-- `CompleteSpace` instance on `untilt p P (Ideal.span {ξ})` when `[Fact ξ.IsPrimitive]`. -/
instance instCompleteSpace [hξ : Fact ξ.IsPrimitive] :
    CompleteSpace (untilt p P (Ideal.span {ξ})) :=
  completeSpace hξ.out

end Complete

end untilt

/-! ### The sharp map and Fontaine's map `θ_J` -/

namespace untilt

section Theta

variable {p} [TopologicalSpace R] [IsTopologicalRing R] [IsHuberRing R] {P : Pair R}
  (J : Ideal (WittVector p P.plus))

variable (p P) in
noncomputable instance instAlgebraWittVector : Algebra (𝕎 P.plus) (untilt p P J) :=
  inferInstanceAs
    (Algebra (𝕎 P.plus) (Localization ((untiltDenominators p P).map (Ideal.Quotient.mk J))))

variable (p P) in
instance instIsScalarTower : IsScalarTower (𝕎 P.plus) (𝕎 P.plus ⧸ J) (untilt p P J) :=
  inferInstanceAs (IsScalarTower (𝕎 P.plus) (𝕎 P.plus ⧸ J)
    (Localization ((untiltDenominators p P).map (Ideal.Quotient.mk J))))

/-- The image of a Witt vector in the untilt is the image of its class modulo `J`. -/
theorem algebraMap_apply (a : 𝕎 P.plus) :
    algebraMap (𝕎 P.plus) (untilt p P J) a =
      algebraMap (𝕎 P.plus ⧸ J) (untilt p P J) (Ideal.Quotient.mk J a) :=
  IsScalarTower.algebraMap_apply _ _ _ a

/-- The image of a Witt vector in the untilt lies in `A⁺`. -/
theorem algebraMap_mem_untiltPlus (a : 𝕎 P.plus) :
    algebraMap (𝕎 P.plus) (untilt p P J) a ∈ untiltPlus p P J := by
  rw [algebraMap_apply]
  exact RingHom.mem_range_self _ _

/-- Every element of `A⁺` is the image of a Witt vector. -/
theorem exists_algebraMap_eq (y : untiltPlus p P J) :
    ∃ a : 𝕎 P.plus, (⟨algebraMap (𝕎 P.plus) _ a, algebraMap_mem_untiltPlus _ a⟩ :
      untiltPlus p P J) = y := by
  obtain ⟨b, hb⟩ := mem_untiltPlus.mp y.property
  obtain ⟨a, rfl⟩ := Ideal.Quotient.mk_surjective b
  exact ⟨a, Subtype.ext ((algebraMap_apply J a).trans hb)⟩

variable (p P) in
/-- The *sharp map on `R⁺`*, `R⁺ → A`, `x ↦ x♯ = θ_J([x])`: the image of the Teichmüller
representative. It is multiplicative and sends `0` to `0`, but it is not additive in general. For
a Tate ring `R` it extends to `R` (`TauCeti.Perfectoid.untilt.sharp`). -/
noncomputable def sharpPlus : P.plus →*₀ untilt p P J where
  __ := (algebraMap (𝕎 P.plus) (untilt p P J) : 𝕎 P.plus →* untilt p P J).comp (teichmuller p)
  map_zero' := by
    simp only [MonoidHom.toFun_eq_coe, MonoidHom.comp_apply, MonoidHom.coe_ofClass,
      WittVector.teichmuller_zero, map_zero]

/-- `x♯` is the image of the Teichmüller representative `[x]`. -/
theorem sharpPlus_apply (x : P.plus) :
    sharpPlus p P J x = algebraMap (𝕎 P.plus) (untilt p P J) (teichmuller p x) :=
  (rfl)

/-- Every `x♯` lies in `A⁺`. -/
theorem sharpPlus_mem_untiltPlus (x : P.plus) : sharpPlus p P J x ∈ untiltPlus p P J :=
  algebraMap_mem_untiltPlus J _

variable {ϖ : P.plus} (hϖ : IsPseudoUniformizer (ϖ : R)) (L : Type*) [CommRing L]
  [Algebra (WittVector p P.plus) L] [IsLocalization.Away (teichmuller p ϖ) L]

/-- **Fontaine's map** `θ_J : 𝕎 R⁺ [1/[ϖ]] → (𝕎 R⁺ ⧸ J)[1/[ϖ]]`, induced by the quotient map
`𝕎 R⁺ → 𝕎 R⁺ ⧸ J`, for a pseudouniformiser `ϖ ∈ R⁺`. Here `L` is any localization of `𝕎 R⁺`
away from `[ϖ]`. -/
noncomputable def theta : L →+* untilt p P J :=
  haveI := isLocalizationAway (J := J) hϖ
  IsLocalization.Away.map L (untilt p P J) (Ideal.Quotient.mk J) (teichmuller p ϖ)

/-- `θ_J` extends the map `𝕎 R⁺ → A`. -/
@[simp]
theorem theta_algebraMap (a : 𝕎 P.plus) :
    theta J hϖ L (algebraMap (𝕎 P.plus) L a) = algebraMap (𝕎 P.plus) (untilt p P J) a := by
  have := isLocalizationAway (J := J) hϖ
  rw [theta, IsLocalization.Away.map, IsLocalization.map_eq, algebraMap_apply]

/-- `θ_J` is surjective. -/
theorem theta_surjective : Function.Surjective (theta J hϖ L) :=
  haveI := isLocalizationAway (J := J) hϖ
  IsLocalization.map_surjective_of_surjective _ _ _ Ideal.Quotient.mk_surjective

/-- **The kernel of `θ_J`** is the ideal generated by `J` in `𝕎 R⁺ [1/[ϖ]]`. -/
theorem ker_theta : RingHom.ker (theta J hϖ L) = J.map (algebraMap (𝕎 P.plus) L) := by
  have := isLocalizationAway (J := J) hϖ
  rw [theta, IsLocalization.Away.map,
    IsLocalization.ker_map (untilt p P J) _ (Submonoid.map_powers _ _), Ideal.mk_ker]

/-- **The untilt is `𝕎 R⁺ [1/[ϖ]] ⧸ J`**: `θ_J` identifies the quotient of `𝕎 R⁺ [1/[ϖ]]` by
the ideal generated by `J` with `(𝕎 R⁺ ⧸ J)[1/[ϖ]]`. -/
noncomputable def quotientMapEquiv : L ⧸ J.map (algebraMap (𝕎 P.plus) L) ≃+* untilt p P J :=
  (Ideal.quotEquivOfEq (ker_theta J hϖ L).symm).trans
    (RingHom.quotientKerEquivOfSurjective (theta_surjective J hϖ L))

/-- `quotientMapEquiv` is induced by `θ_J`. -/
@[simp]
theorem quotientMapEquiv_mk (x : L) :
    quotientMapEquiv J hϖ L (Ideal.Quotient.mk _ x) = theta J hϖ L x :=
  (rfl)

end Theta

/-! ### The sharp map on a Tate ring -/

section Tate

variable {p} [TopologicalSpace R] [IsTopologicalRing R] [IsTateRing R] {P : Pair R}
  {J : Ideal (WittVector p P.plus)}

private theorem isUnit_sharpPlus (x : (IsUnit.submonoid R).comap P.plus.subtype) :
    IsUnit (sharpPlus p P J (x : P.plus)) := by
  rw [sharpPlus_apply, algebraMap_apply]
  exact IsLocalization.map_units (untilt p P J)
    (⟨_, Submonoid.mem_map_of_mem _ (mem_untiltDenominators.mpr
      ⟨x, (IsUnit.mem_submonoid_iff _).mp (Submonoid.mem_comap.mp x.property), rfl⟩)⟩ :
      (untiltDenominators p P).map (Ideal.Quotient.mk J))

variable (P) in
/-- `R` as the localisation of `R⁺` at the elements of `R⁺` that are units of `R`
(`TauCeti.Huber.IsRingOfIntegralElements.isLocalization`). -/
private noncomputable def plusLocalizationMap :
    ((IsUnit.submonoid R).comap P.plus.subtype).LocalizationMap R :=
  haveI := P.isRingOfIntegralElements.isLocalization
  IsLocalization.toLocalizationMap _ R

private theorem plusLocalizationMap_apply (x : P.plus) : plusLocalizationMap P x = x := by
  simp [plusLocalizationMap, Algebra.algebraMap_ofSubsemiring_apply]

variable (p P J) in
/-- **The sharp map `♯_J : R → untilt p P J`.** On `x ∈ R⁺` it is the class `θ_J([x])` of the
Teichmüller representative `[x]` (`TauCeti.Perfectoid.untilt.sharp_apply`), that is
`TauCeti.Perfectoid.untilt.sharpPlus` (`TauCeti.Perfectoid.untilt.sharp_coe`); it is extended to
`R` multiplicatively, every element of `R` being a quotient of an element of `R⁺` by a unit of `R`
lying in `R⁺`. It is multiplicative and sends zero to zero, but is not additive in general. -/
noncomputable def sharp : R →*₀ untilt p P J :=
  (plusLocalizationMap P).lift₀ (sharpPlus p P J) isUnit_sharpPlus

/-- On `R⁺`, the sharp map `♯_J` is `x ↦ x♯`. -/
theorem sharp_coe (x : P.plus) : sharp p P J x = sharpPlus p P J x := by
  rw [sharp, Submonoid.LocalizationMap.lift₀_def, ← plusLocalizationMap_apply,
    Submonoid.LocalizationMap.lift_eq, MonoidHom.coe_ofClass]

/-- **The sharp map on `R⁺`**: `♯_J x` is the class of the Teichmüller representative `[x]`. -/
@[simp]
theorem sharp_apply (x : P.plus) :
    sharp p P J x =
      algebraMap (𝕎 P.plus ⧸ J) (untilt p P J) (Ideal.Quotient.mk J (teichmuller p x)) := by
  rw [sharp_coe, sharpPlus_apply, algebraMap_apply]

/-- **Uniqueness of the sharp map**: a multiplicative map `R → untilt p P J` which sends each
`x ∈ R⁺` to the class of `[x]` is `♯_J`. -/
theorem sharp_unique {f : R →* untilt p P J}
    (hf : ∀ x : P.plus, f x = algebraMap (𝕎 P.plus ⧸ J) (untilt p P J)
      (Ideal.Quotient.mk J (teichmuller p x))) :
    f = (sharp p P J : R →* untilt p P J) := by
  ext x
  rw [MonoidHom.coe_ofClass, sharp, Submonoid.LocalizationMap.lift₀_def]
  exact DFunLike.congr_fun ((plusLocalizationMap P).lift_unique _ fun y ↦ by
    rw [plusLocalizationMap_apply, hf, MonoidHom.coe_ofClass, sharpPlus_apply,
      algebraMap_apply]).symm x

/-- The sharp map sends `R⁺` into `A⁺`. -/
theorem sharp_mem_untiltPlus (x : P.plus) : sharp p P J x ∈ untiltPlus p P J := by
  simp

/-- **The sharp image of a pseudouniformiser is a pseudouniformiser** of the untilt. -/
theorem isPseudoUniformizer_sharp {ϖ : P.plus} (hϖ : IsPseudoUniformizer (ϖ : R)) :
    IsPseudoUniformizer (sharp p P J ϖ) := by
  rw [sharp_apply]
  exact isPseudoUniformizer_algebraMap hϖ

/-- If `J` contains `p - [t]`, then `♯_J t = p`. For instance `♯_J (p♭) = p` for
`J = (p - [p♭]) ⊆ 𝕎 𝒪_{ℂ_p♭}`. -/
theorem sharp_eq_natCast {t : P.plus} (ht : (p : 𝕎 P.plus) - teichmuller p t ∈ J) :
    sharp p P J t = p := by
  rw [sharp_apply, ← Ideal.Quotient.eq.mpr ht, map_natCast, map_natCast]

end Tate

/-! ### The untilt along `(p)` -/

section SpanP

variable {p} [TopologicalSpace R] [IsTopologicalRing R] [IsHuberRing R] [CharP R p]
  [PerfectRing R p] {P : Pair R} {ϖ : P.plus} (hϖ : IsPseudoUniformizer (ϖ : R)) (L : Type*)
  [CommRing L] [Algebra P.plus L] [IsLocalization.Away ϖ L]

/-- **The untilt along `(p)` is `R⁺[1/ϖ]`**: for `R` perfect of characteristic `p`, reduction of
the zeroth Witt coordinate identifies `𝕎 R⁺ ⧸ (p)` with `R⁺`, and hence the untilt along `(p)`
with any localization `L` of `R⁺` away from a pseudouniformiser `ϖ`. -/
noncomputable def spanPEquiv : untilt p P (Ideal.span {(p : 𝕎 P.plus)}) ≃+* L :=
  haveI := isLocalizationAway (J := Ideal.span {(p : 𝕎 P.plus)}) hϖ
  IsLocalization.ringEquivOfRingEquiv (M := Submonoid.powers
      (Ideal.Quotient.mk (Ideal.span {(p : 𝕎 P.plus)}) (teichmuller p ϖ)))
    (T := Submonoid.powers ϖ) (untilt p P (Ideal.span {(p : 𝕎 P.plus)})) L
    WittVector.quotientPEquiv <| by
      rw [Submonoid.map_powers]
      exact congrArg Submonoid.powers ((WittVector.quotientPEquiv_mk _).trans
        ((WittVector.constantCoeff_apply _).trans (WittVector.teichmuller_coeff_zero _ ϖ)))

/-- `spanPEquiv` sends the image of a Witt vector `a` to its zeroth Witt coordinate. -/
@[simp]
theorem spanPEquiv_algebraMap (a : 𝕎 P.plus) :
    spanPEquiv hϖ L (algebraMap (𝕎 P.plus) _ a) = algebraMap P.plus L (a.coeff 0) := by
  have := isLocalizationAway (J := Ideal.span {(p : 𝕎 P.plus)}) hϖ
  have h := WittVector.quotientPEquiv_mk a
  simp only [Submodule.Quotient.quot_mk_eq_mk, Ideal.Quotient.mk_eq_mk] at h
  rw [algebraMap_apply, spanPEquiv, IsLocalization.ringEquivOfRingEquiv_eq, h,
    WittVector.constantCoeff_apply]

/-- `spanPEquiv` sends `x♯` to `x`. -/
@[simp]
theorem spanPEquiv_sharpPlus (x : P.plus) :
    spanPEquiv hϖ L (sharpPlus p P _ x) = algebraMap P.plus L x := by
  rw [sharpPlus_apply, spanPEquiv_algebraMap, WittVector.teichmuller_coeff_zero]

/-- The inverse of `spanPEquiv` sends `x` to `x♯`. -/
@[simp]
theorem spanPEquiv_symm_algebraMap (x : P.plus) :
    (spanPEquiv hϖ L).symm (algebraMap P.plus L x) = sharpPlus p P _ x := by
  rw [RingEquiv.symm_apply_eq, spanPEquiv_sharpPlus]

end SpanP

/-! ### The ring `A⁺` along a primitive element -/

section PrimitivePlus

variable {p} [TopologicalSpace R] [IsTopologicalRing R] [IsTateRing R] [CharP R p]
  [PerfectRing R p] {P : Pair R} {ξ : WittVector p P.plus}

/-- **`A⁺ = 𝕎 R⁺ ⧸ (ξ)`** for the untilt along a primitive element `ξ`, for `R` a perfect Tate
ring of characteristic `p`. -/
noncomputable def quotientEquivUntiltPlus (hξ : ξ.IsPrimitive) :
    𝕎 P.plus ⧸ Ideal.span {ξ} ≃+* untiltPlus p P (Ideal.span {ξ}) :=
  RingEquiv.ofBijective (algebraMap (𝕎 P.plus ⧸ Ideal.span {ξ}) _).rangeRestrict
    ⟨(algebraMap_injective hξ).codRestrict _, RingHom.rangeRestrict_surjective _⟩

/-- `quotientEquivUntiltPlus` is the map to the untilt. -/
@[simp]
theorem coe_quotientEquivUntiltPlus_apply (hξ : ξ.IsPrimitive) (a : 𝕎 P.plus ⧸ Ideal.span {ξ}) :
    (quotientEquivUntiltPlus hξ a : untilt p P (Ideal.span {ξ})) =
      algebraMap (𝕎 P.plus ⧸ Ideal.span {ξ}) _ a :=
  (rfl)

/-- `quotientEquivUntiltPlus` carries the class of `[a]` to `sharp a`. -/
@[simp]
theorem quotientEquivUntiltPlus_mk_teichmuller (hξ : ξ.IsPrimitive) (a : P.plus) :
    quotientEquivUntiltPlus hξ (Ideal.Quotient.mk (Ideal.span {ξ}) (teichmuller p a)) =
      ⟨sharp p P (Ideal.span {ξ}) a, sharp_mem_untiltPlus a⟩ :=
  Subtype.ext ((coe_quotientEquivUntiltPlus_apply hξ _).trans (sharp_apply a).symm)

/-- **`A⁺ ⧸ (♯ϖ) ≃+* R⁺ ⧸ (ϖ)`** for the untilt along a primitive element `ξ`, for every
`ϖ ∈ R⁺` dividing the zeroth Witt coordinate of `ξ`. It is induced by the zeroth Witt
coordinate (`TauCeti.Perfectoid.untilt.quotientSharpEquiv_mk`), and sends the class of `♯x` to
the class of `x` (`TauCeti.Perfectoid.untilt.quotientSharpEquiv_mk_sharp`). -/
noncomputable def quotientSharpEquiv (hξ : ξ.IsPrimitive) {ϖ : P.plus} (hξ₀ : ϖ ∣ ξ.coeff 0) :
    untiltPlus p P (Ideal.span {ξ}) ⧸
        Ideal.span {(⟨sharp p P _ ϖ, sharp_mem_untiltPlus ϖ⟩ : untiltPlus p P (Ideal.span {ξ}))} ≃+*
      P.plus ⧸ Ideal.span {ϖ} :=
  (Ideal.quotientEquiv _ _ (quotientEquivUntiltPlus hξ) (by
    rw [Ideal.map_span, Set.image_singleton]
    congr 2
    exact Subtype.ext (sharp_apply ϖ))).symm.trans
    (hξ.isDistinguished.quotientTeichmullerEquiv hξ₀)

/-- `quotientSharpEquiv` sends the class of the image of a Witt vector `a` to the class of its
zeroth Witt coordinate. -/
@[simp]
theorem quotientSharpEquiv_mk (hξ : ξ.IsPrimitive) {ϖ : P.plus} (hξ₀ : ϖ ∣ ξ.coeff 0)
    (a : 𝕎 P.plus) :
    quotientSharpEquiv hξ hξ₀
        (Ideal.Quotient.mk _ ⟨algebraMap (𝕎 P.plus) _ a, algebraMap_mem_untiltPlus _ a⟩) =
      Ideal.Quotient.mk _ (a.coeff 0) := by
  have ha : (⟨algebraMap (𝕎 P.plus) _ a, algebraMap_mem_untiltPlus _ a⟩ :
      untiltPlus p P (Ideal.span {ξ})) = quotientEquivUntiltPlus hξ (Ideal.Quotient.mk _ a) :=
    Subtype.ext (algebraMap_apply _ a)
  rw [ha, quotientSharpEquiv, RingEquiv.trans_apply, Ideal.quotientEquiv_symm_mk,
    RingEquiv.symm_apply_apply, WittVector.IsDistinguished.quotientTeichmullerEquiv_mk_mk]

/-- **Divisibility by `♯ϖ` in `A⁺`** for the untilt along a primitive element `ξ`: for every
`ϖ ∈ R⁺` dividing the zeroth Witt coordinate of `ξ`, `♯ϖ` divides the image of a Witt vector `a`
in `A⁺` exactly when `ϖ` divides the zeroth Witt coordinate of `a`. -/
theorem sharp_dvd_algebraMap_iff (hξ : ξ.IsPrimitive) {ϖ : P.plus} (hξ₀ : ϖ ∣ ξ.coeff 0)
    (a : 𝕎 P.plus) :
    (⟨sharp p P _ ϖ, sharp_mem_untiltPlus ϖ⟩ : untiltPlus p P (Ideal.span {ξ})) ∣
        ⟨algebraMap (𝕎 P.plus) _ a, algebraMap_mem_untiltPlus _ a⟩ ↔
      ϖ ∣ a.coeff 0 := by
  rw [← Ideal.mem_span_singleton, ← Ideal.Quotient.eq_zero_iff_mem,
    ← map_eq_zero_iff (quotientSharpEquiv hξ hξ₀) (EquivLike.injective _), quotientSharpEquiv_mk,
    Ideal.Quotient.eq_zero_iff_mem, Ideal.mem_span_singleton]

/-- `quotientSharpEquiv` sends the class of the image of `a ∈ 𝕎 R⁺`, written through
`𝕎 R⁺ ⧸ (ξ)` with any membership proof, to the class of its zeroth Witt coordinate. This is the
form `simp` reaches from `♯x` after `TauCeti.Perfectoid.untilt.sharp_apply`. -/
@[simp]
theorem quotientSharpEquiv_mk_algebraMap (hξ : ξ.IsPrimitive) {ϖ : P.plus}
    (hξ₀ : ϖ ∣ ξ.coeff 0) (a : 𝕎 P.plus)
    (h : algebraMap _ _ (Ideal.Quotient.mk (Ideal.span {ξ}) a) ∈ untiltPlus p P (Ideal.span {ξ})) :
    quotientSharpEquiv hξ hξ₀ (Ideal.Quotient.mk _ ⟨algebraMap _ _ (Ideal.Quotient.mk _ a), h⟩) =
      Ideal.Quotient.mk _ (a.coeff 0) := by
  have he : (⟨_, h⟩ : untiltPlus p P (Ideal.span {ξ})) =
      ⟨algebraMap (𝕎 P.plus) _ a, algebraMap_mem_untiltPlus _ a⟩ :=
    Subtype.ext (algebraMap_apply _ a).symm
  rw [he, quotientSharpEquiv_mk]

/-- `quotientSharpEquiv` sends the class of `♯x` to the class of `x`, for `x ∈ R⁺`. Not
`@[simp]`: `simp` first rewrites `♯x` by `TauCeti.Perfectoid.untilt.sharp_apply`, and then proves
this by `TauCeti.Perfectoid.untilt.quotientSharpEquiv_mk_algebraMap`. -/
theorem quotientSharpEquiv_mk_sharp (hξ : ξ.IsPrimitive) {ϖ : P.plus} (hξ₀ : ϖ ∣ ξ.coeff 0)
    (x : P.plus) :
    quotientSharpEquiv hξ hξ₀ (Ideal.Quotient.mk _ ⟨sharp p P _ x, sharp_mem_untiltPlus x⟩) =
      Ideal.Quotient.mk _ x := by
  simp

/-- The inverse of `quotientSharpEquiv` sends the class of `a` to the class of `sharp a`. -/
@[simp]
theorem quotientSharpEquiv_symm_mk (hξ : ξ.IsPrimitive) {ϖ : P.plus} (hξ₀ : ϖ ∣ ξ.coeff 0)
    (a : P.plus) :
    (quotientSharpEquiv hξ hξ₀).symm (Ideal.Quotient.mk (Ideal.span {ϖ}) a) =
      Ideal.Quotient.mk _ ⟨sharp p P (Ideal.span {ξ}) a, sharp_mem_untiltPlus a⟩ := by
  rw [RingEquiv.symm_apply_eq, quotientSharpEquiv_mk_sharp]

/-- Integral uniform estimate for continuity of `sharp`: when `p` is topologically nilpotent in
`untilt p P J`, `ϖ ^ M ∣ a - b` in `P.plus` puts `sharp a - sharp b` in `π ^ N A⁺`. -/
private theorem sharp_sub_mem_awayNhd_of_dvd {J : Ideal (WittVector p P.plus)}
    (hp : IsTopologicallyNilpotent (p : untilt p P J)) {ϖ : P.plus}
    (hϖ : IsPseudoUniformizer (ϖ : R)) (N : ℕ) :
    ∃ M : ℕ, ∀ a b : P.plus, ϖ ^ M ∣ a - b →
      sharp p P J a - sharp p P J b ∈
        awayNhd (Ideal.Quotient.mk J (teichmuller p ϖ)) (untilt p P J) N := by
  set π₀ : WittVector p P.plus ⧸ J := Ideal.Quotient.mk J (teichmuller p ϖ)
  have hbasis := hasBasis_nhds_zero (J := J) hϖ
  obtain ⟨d, hd⟩ := Filter.eventually_atTop.mp
    (hp.eventually_mem (hbasis.mem_of_mem (i := N) trivial))
  refine ⟨N * p ^ d, fun a b hab ↦ ?_⟩
  set w : WittVector p P.plus := teichmuller p a - teichmuller p b
  -- `ϖ ^ (N * p ^ d) ∣ a - b` forces `ϖ ^ (N * p ^ d) ∣ w.coeff i` for every `i`.
  have hcoeff (i : ℕ) : ϖ ^ (N * p ^ d) ∣ w.coeff i := by
    let q := Ideal.Quotient.mk (Ideal.span {ϖ ^ (N * p ^ d)})
    have hqab : q a = q b := Ideal.Quotient.eq.mpr (Ideal.mem_span_singleton.mpr hab)
    have hmap : WittVector.map q w = 0 := by
      rw [map_sub, map_teichmuller, map_teichmuller, hqab, sub_self]
    have hi : q (w.coeff i) = 0 := by
      simpa [WittVector.map_coeff] using congrArg (WittVector.coeff · i) hmap
    exact Ideal.mem_span_singleton.mp (Ideal.Quotient.eq_zero_iff_mem.mp hi)
  -- Hence the `i`-th Teichmüller coefficient of `w` is divisible by `ϖ ^ N` for `i < d`.
  have htc (i : ℕ) (hi : i < d) : ϖ ^ N ∣ w.teichmullerCoeff i := by
    have hdiv : (ϖ ^ (N * p ^ (d - i))) ^ p ^ i ∣ (w.teichmullerCoeff i) ^ p ^ i := by
      rw [teichmullerCoeff_pow, ← pow_mul, mul_assoc, ← pow_add, Nat.sub_add_cancel hi.le]
      exact hcoeff i
    rw [← iterateFrobeniusEquiv_def, ← iterateFrobeniusEquiv_def] at hdiv
    exact (pow_dvd_pow ϖ (Nat.le_mul_of_pos_right N (pow_pos (Fact.out : p.Prime).pos _))).trans
      ((map_dvd_iff (iterateFrobeniusEquiv P.plus p i)).mp hdiv)
  obtain ⟨b₀, hb₀⟩ := exists_eq_sum_teichmullerCoeff_add_pow_mul w d
  have hsharp_sub : sharp p P J a - sharp p P J b =
      algebraMap (WittVector p P.plus ⧸ J) (untilt p P J) (Ideal.Quotient.mk J w) := by
    rw [sharp_apply, sharp_apply, ← map_sub, ← map_sub]
  rw [hsharp_sub, hb₀, map_add, map_add, map_sum, map_sum]
  refine add_mem (sum_mem fun i hi ↦ ?_) ?_
  · obtain ⟨c, hc⟩ := htc i (Finset.mem_range.mp hi)
    have hteich : teichmuller p (w.teichmullerCoeff i) =
        teichmuller p ϖ ^ N * teichmuller p c := by
      rw [hc, map_mul, map_pow]
    rw [hteich, mul_assoc, map_mul, map_pow]
    exact mem_awayNhd.mpr ⟨_, rfl⟩
  · rw [map_mul, map_pow, map_natCast, map_mul, map_pow, map_natCast, mul_comm]
    simpa using algebraMap_pow_mul_mul_mem_awayNhd (k := 0) (Ideal.Quotient.mk J b₀) (hd d le_rfl)

/-- **Continuity of the sharp map**: if `R` is a perfect Tate ring of characteristic `p` and `p` is
topologically nilpotent in `untilt p P J`, then `sharp p P J : R →*₀ untilt p P J` is
continuous. -/
theorem continuous_sharp_of_isTopologicallyNilpotent {J : Ideal (WittVector p P.plus)}
    (hp : IsTopologicallyNilpotent (p : untilt p P J)) :
    Continuous (sharp p P J) := by
  obtain ⟨ϖ, hϖ⟩ := P.isRingOfIntegralElements.exists_isPseudoUniformizer
  set π₀ : WittVector p P.plus ⧸ J := Ideal.Quotient.mk J (teichmuller p ϖ)
  have hbasis := hasBasis_nhds_zero (J := J) hϖ
  have hπ_unit : IsUnit (algebraMap (WittVector p P.plus ⧸ J) (untilt p P J) π₀) :=
    (isPseudoUniformizer_algebraMap (J := J) hϖ).isUnit
  -- Reduce continuity at `x₀ : R` to the integral estimate by clearing denominators with `ϖ ^ k`.
  refine continuous_iff_continuousAt.mpr fun x₀ ↦ ?_
  rw [ContinuousAt, ← tendsto_sub_nhds_zero_iff, hbasis.tendsto_right_iff]
  intro r _
  obtain ⟨k, hk⟩ := exists_mul_pow_mem_of_isTopologicallyNilpotent
    hϖ.isTopologicallyNilpotent P.isRingOfIntegralElements.isOpen x₀
  obtain ⟨M, hM⟩ := sharp_sub_mem_awayNhd_of_dvd hp hϖ (r + k)
  let V : Set R := (hϖ.isUnit.pow M).unit • (P.plus : Set R)
  have hV : V ∈ 𝓝 (0 : R) := by
    refine (P.isRingOfIntegralElements.isOpen.smul (hϖ.isUnit.pow M).unit).mem_nhds ?_
    exact ⟨0, P.plus.zero_mem, by simp⟩
  have hmem : (fun x : R ↦ x - x₀) ⁻¹' V ∈ 𝓝 x₀ :=
    (continuous_id.sub continuous_const).continuousAt.preimage_mem_nhds (by simpa using hV)
  filter_upwards [hmem] with x hx
  obtain ⟨c, hc, hxc⟩ := Set.mem_smul_set.mp hx
  have hxc' : (ϖ : R) ^ M * c = x - x₀ := by simpa [smul_eq_mul] using hxc
  have hxk : x * (ϖ : R) ^ k ∈ P.plus := by
    have heq : x * (ϖ : R) ^ k = x₀ * (ϖ : R) ^ k + (ϖ : R) ^ M * c * (ϖ : R) ^ k := by
      linear_combination -hxc' * (ϖ : R) ^ k
    rw [heq]
    exact P.plus.add_mem hk (P.plus.mul_mem (P.plus.mul_mem (P.plus.pow_mem ϖ.property M) hc)
      (P.plus.pow_mem ϖ.property k))
  let a : P.plus := ⟨x * (ϖ : R) ^ k, hxk⟩
  let b : P.plus := ⟨x₀ * (ϖ : R) ^ k, hk⟩
  have hdvd : ϖ ^ M ∣ a - b := by
    refine ⟨⟨c, hc⟩ * ϖ ^ k, Subtype.ext ?_⟩
    simp only [AddSubgroupClass.coe_sub, Subring.coe_mul, Subring.coe_pow, a, b]
    linear_combination -hxc' * (ϖ : R) ^ k
  obtain ⟨d, hd⟩ := mem_awayNhd.mp (hM a b hdvd)
  refine mem_awayNhd.mpr ⟨d, (hπ_unit.pow k).mul_right_cancel ?_⟩
  have hax : sharp p P J a = sharp p P J x * sharp p P J (ϖ : R) ^ k := by
    rw [← map_pow, ← map_mul]
  have hbx : sharp p P J b = sharp p P J x₀ * sharp p P J (ϖ : R) ^ k := by
    rw [← map_pow, ← map_mul]
  calc algebraMap (WittVector p P.plus ⧸ J) (untilt p P J) (π₀ ^ r * d) *
        algebraMap (WittVector p P.plus ⧸ J) (untilt p P J) π₀ ^ k
    _ = algebraMap (WittVector p P.plus ⧸ J) (untilt p P J) (π₀ ^ (r + k) * d) := by
        simp only [map_mul, map_pow, π₀, pow_add]
        ring
    _ = sharp p P J a - sharp p P J b := hd
    _ = (sharp p P J x - sharp p P J x₀) *
          algebraMap (WittVector p P.plus ⧸ J) (untilt p P J) π₀ ^ k := by
        rw [hax, hbx, sharp_apply ϖ, ← sub_mul]

/-- In the untilt along a primitive element `ξ`, `p` is topologically nilpotent. -/
theorem isTopologicallyNilpotent_natCast (hξ : ξ.IsPrimitive) :
    IsTopologicallyNilpotent (p : untilt p P (Ideal.span {ξ})) := by
  obtain ⟨ϖ, hϖ⟩ := P.isRingOfIntegralElements.exists_isPseudoUniformizer
  set J := Ideal.span {ξ}
  obtain ⟨n, d, hd⟩ := hξ.isDistinguished.exists_mk_teichmuller_dvd_natCast_pow
    (hξ.coeff_zero_mem_radical hϖ)
  have hpow : (p : untilt p P J) ^ (n + 1) =
      algebraMap (WittVector p P.plus ⧸ J) (untilt p P J) (Ideal.Quotient.mk J (teichmuller p ϖ)) *
        algebraMap (WittVector p P.plus ⧸ J) (untilt p P J) d := by
    rw [← map_mul, ← hd, map_pow, map_natCast]
  refine IsTopologicallyNilpotent.of_pow n.succ_ne_zero ?_
  rw [hpow, mul_comm]
  exact (isBounded_untiltPlus.isPowerBounded_of_mem
    (mem_untiltPlus.mpr ⟨d, rfl⟩)).isTopologicallyNilpotent_mul
    (isPseudoUniformizer_algebraMap hϖ).isTopologicallyNilpotent

/-- `p` is topologically nilpotent in the untilt along a primitive element. -/
instance instFactIsTopologicallyNilpotentNatCast [hξ : Fact ξ.IsPrimitive] :
    Fact (IsTopologicallyNilpotent (p : untilt p P (Ideal.span {ξ}))) :=
  ⟨isTopologicallyNilpotent_natCast hξ.out⟩

/-- **The sharp map is continuous** along a primitive element `ξ`, for `R` a perfect Tate ring of
characteristic `p`. -/
theorem continuous_sharp (hξ : ξ.IsPrimitive) : Continuous (sharp p P (Ideal.span {ξ})) :=
  continuous_sharp_of_isTopologicallyNilpotent (isTopologicallyNilpotent_natCast hξ)

end PrimitivePlus

section CompletePlus

variable {p} [UniformSpace R] [IsUniformAddGroup R] [IsTopologicalRing R] [IsTateRing R]
  [CompleteSpace R] [T2Space R] [CharP R p] [PerfectRing R p] {P : Pair R}
  {ξ : WittVector p P.plus}

/-- For primitive `ξ`, `A⁺` is `p`-adically complete. -/
theorem isAdicComplete_untiltPlus_natCast (hξ : ξ.IsPrimitive) :
    IsAdicComplete (Ideal.span {(p : untiltPlus p P (Ideal.span {ξ}))})
      (untiltPlus p P (Ideal.span {ξ})) := by
  have := isAdicComplete_quotient_natCast hξ
  have hmap : (Ideal.span {(p : 𝕎 P.plus ⧸ Ideal.span {ξ})}).map
      (quotientEquivUntiltPlus hξ) =
      Ideal.span {(p : untiltPlus p P (Ideal.span {ξ}))} := by
    rw [Ideal.map_span, Set.image_singleton, map_natCast]
  exact hmap ▸ (IsAdicComplete.congr_ringEquiv
    (Ideal.span {(p : 𝕎 P.plus ⧸ Ideal.span {ξ})}) (quotientEquivUntiltPlus hξ)).mpr inferInstance

/-- `IsAdicComplete` instance for `(p)` on `A⁺` when `[Fact ξ.IsPrimitive]`. -/
instance instIsAdicCompleteUntiltPlusNatCast [hξ : Fact ξ.IsPrimitive] :
    IsAdicComplete (Ideal.span {(p : untiltPlus p P (Ideal.span {ξ}))})
      (untiltPlus p P (Ideal.span {ξ})) :=
  isAdicComplete_untiltPlus_natCast hξ.out

/-- In a nontrivial primitive untilt, `p` is not a unit of `A⁺`. -/
theorem not_isUnit_untiltPlus_natCast (hξ : ξ.IsPrimitive)
    [Nontrivial (untilt p P (Ideal.span {ξ}))] :
    ¬IsUnit (p : untiltPlus p P (Ideal.span {ξ})) :=
  have := isAdicComplete_untiltPlus_natCast hξ
  have : Nontrivial (untiltPlus p P (Ideal.span {ξ})) :=
    (untiltPlus p P (Ideal.span {ξ})).subtype.domain_nontrivial
  IsAdicComplete.not_isUnit_of_mem (Ideal.mem_span_singleton_self _)

/-- `Fact ¬IsUnit (p : A⁺)` instance when `[Fact ξ.IsPrimitive]` and `A` is nontrivial. -/
instance instFactNotIsUnitUntiltPlusNatCast [hξ : Fact ξ.IsPrimitive]
    [Nontrivial (untilt p P (Ideal.span {ξ}))] :
    Fact ¬IsUnit (p : untiltPlus p P (Ideal.span {ξ})) :=
  ⟨not_isUnit_untiltPlus_natCast hξ.out⟩

end CompletePlus

/-! ### The untilt along a primitive element is perfectoid -/

section Perfectoid

variable {p} [UniformSpace R] [IsUniformAddGroup R] [IsTopologicalRing R] [IsTateRing R]
  [CompleteSpace R] [T2Space R] [CharP R p] [PerfectRing R p] {P : Pair R}
  {ξ : WittVector p P.plus}

/-- **The untilt along a primitive element is a perfectoid Tate ring** (Scholze, *Étale cohomology
of diamonds*, Theorem 3.17 and its proof; Kedlaya, *Sheaves, stacks, and shtukas*,
Theorem 2.3.9): for `R` a perfect complete Hausdorff Tate ring of characteristic `p`, a Huber pair
`(R, R⁺)` and a primitive `ξ ∈ 𝕎 R⁺`, the untilt `(𝕎 R⁺ ⧸ (ξ))[1/[ϖ]]` is a perfectoid Tate ring.
Its complete Hausdorff structure is `TauCeti.Perfectoid.untilt.completeSpace` and
`TauCeti.Perfectoid.untilt.t2Space`. -/
theorem isPerfectoidTateRing (hξ : ξ.IsPrimitive) :
    haveI := completeSpace hξ
    haveI := t2Space hξ
    IsPerfectoidTateRing p (untilt p P (Ideal.span {ξ})) := by
  have := completeSpace hξ
  have := t2Space hξ
  have hp : p.Prime := Fact.out
  obtain ⟨ϖ, hϖ, hϖξ⟩ := hξ.exists_isPseudoUniformizer_pow_dvd_coeff_zero
  -- `A⁺` is open and bounded, and Frobenius `A⁺ ⧸ (♯ϖ) → A⁺ ⧸ (♯ϖ ^ p)` is bijective, since it
  -- is Frobenius `R⁺ ⧸ (ϖ) → R⁺ ⧸ (ϖ ^ p)` under `quotientSharpEquiv`
  set π : untiltPlus p P (Ideal.span {ξ}) := ⟨sharp p P _ ϖ, sharp_mem_untiltPlus ϖ⟩
  have hπp : π ^ p = ⟨sharp p P _ ↑(ϖ ^ p), sharp_mem_untiltPlus (ϖ ^ p)⟩ :=
    Subtype.ext (by simp only [π, SubmonoidClass.coe_pow, map_pow])
  have hdvd (a : 𝕎 P.plus) : π ^ p ∣ ⟨algebraMap (𝕎 P.plus) _ a, algebraMap_mem_untiltPlus _ a⟩ ↔
      ϖ ^ p ∣ a.coeff 0 := by
    rw [hπp, sharp_dvd_algebraMap_iff hξ hϖξ]
  have h : π ^ p ∣ (p : untiltPlus p P (Ideal.span {ξ})) := by
    have hpa : (p : untiltPlus p P (Ideal.span {ξ})) =
        ⟨algebraMap (𝕎 P.plus) _ p, algebraMap_mem_untiltPlus _ _⟩ :=
      Subtype.ext (by simp)
    rw [hpa, hdvd, ← WittVector.constantCoeff_apply, map_natCast, CharP.cast_eq_zero]
    exact dvd_zero _
  refine IsPerfectoidTateRing.of_bijective_frobeniusModPow isOpen_untiltPlus isBounded_untiltPlus
    (isPseudoUniformizer_sharp hϖ) h ⟨(frobeniusModPow_injective_iff h).mpr fun y hy ↦ ?_,
      (frobeniusModPow_surjective_iff h).mpr fun x ↦ ?_⟩
  · obtain ⟨a, rfl⟩ := exists_algebraMap_eq _ y
    have hy' : π ^ p ∣ ⟨algebraMap (𝕎 P.plus) _ (a ^ p), algebraMap_mem_untiltPlus _ _⟩ := by
      simpa using hy
    rw [hdvd, ← WittVector.constantCoeff_apply, map_pow, WittVector.constantCoeff_apply] at hy'
    rw [sharp_dvd_algebraMap_iff hξ ((dvd_pow_self ϖ hp.ne_zero).trans hϖξ)]
    simpa using map_dvd (frobeniusEquiv P.plus p).symm hy'
  · obtain ⟨a, rfl⟩ := exists_algebraMap_eq _ x
    refine ⟨⟨sharp p P _ ((frobeniusEquiv P.plus p).symm (a.coeff 0)),
      sharp_mem_untiltPlus _⟩, ?_⟩
    have hsub : (⟨algebraMap (𝕎 P.plus) _ a, algebraMap_mem_untiltPlus _ a⟩ :
        untiltPlus p P (Ideal.span {ξ})) - ⟨sharp p P _
          ((frobeniusEquiv P.plus p).symm (a.coeff 0)), sharp_mem_untiltPlus _⟩ ^ p =
        ⟨algebraMap (𝕎 P.plus) _ (a - teichmuller p (a.coeff 0)), algebraMap_mem_untiltPlus _ _⟩ :=
      Subtype.ext (by
        simp only [AddSubgroupClass.coe_sub, SubmonoidClass.coe_pow]
        rw [← map_pow, ← SubmonoidClass.coe_pow, frobeniusEquiv_symm_pow_p, sharp_apply,
          ← algebraMap_apply, map_sub])
    rw [hsub, hdvd, ← WittVector.constantCoeff_apply, map_sub, WittVector.constantCoeff_apply,
      WittVector.constantCoeff_apply, WittVector.teichmuller_coeff_zero, sub_self]
    exact dvd_zero _

end Perfectoid

end untilt

end TauCeti.Perfectoid
